741	test_condition_001	2025-12-20 14:02:41.706082	What is the difference between Fair and Superb condition? (no changes needed)	The difference between **Fair** and **Superb** condition in our refurbished devices primarily relates to their cosmetic appearance and battery health. Here's a breakdown for clarity:\n\n### **Superb Condition:**\n- **Cosmetic Condition:** Near-mint, may have extremely faint, hardly noticeable scratches.\n- **Battery Health:** 85% and above.\n- **Performance:** Fully functional, passes every diagnostic test.\n- **Who It's For:** Great for users seeking a near-new experience or those looking to gift a device.\n\n### **Fair Condition:**\n- **Cosmetic Condition:** Noticeable scratches, scuffs, or visible wear, but fully functional.\n- **Battery Health:** 80% and above.\n- **Performance:** Fully functional, passed all hardware diagnostics but has aesthetic flaws.\n- **Who It's For:** Best for budget-conscious buyers who need a reliable device for daily use, with less concern for appearance.\n\nThis grading system helps you choose based on your specific needs and budget! If you have more questions or would like help choosing, feel free to ask! 😊\n\n---\n\n*Here are some helpful links:*\n[All Products](https://grest.in/collections/all) | [iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/[iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/iphones)) | [MacBooks](https://grest.in/collections/[MacBooks](https://grest.in/collections/macbook))\n\n---\n\n*Here are some helpful links:*\n[iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/iphones) | [All Products](https://grest.in/collections/all) | [MacBooks](https://grest.in/collections/macbook)	f	\N	["https://grest.in/blogs/news/refurbished-iphone-conditions-fair-good-superb", "https://grest.in/blogs/news/trade-in-vs-buying-a-refurbished-iphone-which-route-gives-you-better-value", "https://grest.in/pages/faqs"]	\N	\N
