793	test_condition_001	2025-12-20 14:13:22.407636	What is the difference between Fair and Superb condition? (no changes needed)	The difference between **Fair** and **Superb** condition in refurbished devices primarily relates to their cosmetic appearance and battery health. Here’s a breakdown:\n\n- **Superb Condition:**\n  - **Cosmetic Condition:** Near-mint condition with minimal signs of use.\n  - **Battery Health:** 85% and above.\n  - **Performance:** 100% functional, fully tested and certified.\n  \n- **Fair Condition:**\n  - **Cosmetic Condition:** Noticeable scratches, scuffs, or visible wear, but fully functional.\n  - **Battery Health:** 80% and above.\n  - **Performance:** Fully functional and passes all hardware diagnostics, but with more cosmetic flaws compared to Superb.\n\nBoth conditions maintain excellent performance, but the Superb condition offers a more pristine aesthetic and better battery health. If you’re looking for a “like-new” experience, go for Superb. If your priority is cost savings and function, Fair might be a better fit.\n\nIf you have more questions or need help choosing a device, feel free to ask! 😊\n\n---\n\n*Browse more options here:*\n[All Products](https://grest.in/collections/all) | [iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/iphones) | [MacBooks](https://grest.in/collections/macbook)	f	\N	["https://grest.in/blogs/news/refurbished-iphone-conditions-fair-good-superb", "https://grest.in/pages/faqs", "https://grest.in/blogs/news/trade-in-vs-buying-a-refurbished-iphone-which-route-gives-you-better-value"]	\N	\N
