842	test_condition_001	2025-12-20 23:28:20.512433	What is the difference between Fair and Superb condition?	**Great question!** Let's break down the differences between **Fair** and **Superb** conditions for our refurbished [iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/iphones):\n\n### **Fair Condition:**\n- **Appearance:** Noticeable scratches, scuffs, or visible wear. Marks on the frame or screen are clearly visible, but all are purely cosmetic.\n- **Battery Health:** Minimum 80% battery health.\n- **Performance:** Fully functional, having passed all hardware diagnostics.\n\n### **Superb Condition:**\n- **Appearance:** Almost new look, with minimal to no visible wear. There may be extremely faint, hardly noticeable hairline scratches.\n- **Battery Health:** Battery health is 85% and above.\n- **Performance:** 100% functional, passing every diagnostic test with excellent longevity.\n\nIn summary, **Superb condition** provides a like-new experience with higher battery health and better aesthetics, while **Fair condition** offers solid functionality with clear signs of previous use.\n\nIf you have any specific model in mind, feel free to ask, and we can provide more details! 😊\n\n---\n\n*You might also like to check:*\n[iPhones](https://grest.in/collections/iphones) | [All Products](https://grest.in/collections/all) | [About Us](https://grest.in/pages/about)	f	\N	["https://grest.in/blogs/news/refurbished-iphone-conditions-fair-good-superb", "https://grest.in/pages/faqs", "grest_product_catalog.txt"]	\N	\N
